From c736e2259046d584533bd606ef7e05d98c6332a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 22:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 099/145] media: meson: vdec: do not dereference a session the
 teardown already cleared

vdec_isr() and vdec_threaded_isr() both take core->cur_sess and use it
without checking it:

	struct amvdec_session *sess = core->cur_sess;
	sess->last_irq_jiffies = get_jiffies_64();
	return sess->fmt_out->codec_ops->isr(sess);

vdec_stop_streaming() sets core->cur_sess = NULL while the decoder's
interrupt is still requested and the hardware may still have one to
raise.  A late interrupt then writes through a NULL pointer in the hard
handler before it can reach any codec at all.  The interrupt is also
shared-capable in the sense that it stays requested for the lifetime of
the driver, so a spurious one outside any session hits the same path.

Return IRQ_NONE instead, which is what a handler with no work owes the
core.

This does not close the whole teardown window - a session freed after
cur_sess is read is still a use-after-free, and the structural fix is to
quiesce the threaded handler (synchronize_irq()) before vdec_poweroff()
frees anything.  That needs the irq number kept in amvdec_core, which it
currently is not, and it needs care not to deadlock against a handler
blocked on a codec lock, so it is left for a separate change.  This one
is the unconditional NULL dereference, which needs no timing at all.

Fixes: 3e7f51bd9607 ("media: meson: add v4l2 m2m video decoder driver")
Signed-off-by: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
index dd15d9894255..e324320b3d8a 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
@@ -1175,6 +1175,15 @@ static irqreturn_t vdec_isr(int irq, void *data)
 {
 	struct amvdec_core *core = data;
 	struct amvdec_session *sess = core->cur_sess;
+
+	/*
+	 * vdec_stop_streaming() clears cur_sess while the hardware may still
+	 * have an interrupt to raise - a late or spurious one then arrives
+	 * with no session at all.
+	 */
+	if (!sess)
+		return IRQ_NONE;
+
 	sess->last_irq_jiffies = get_jiffies_64();
 
 	return sess->fmt_out->codec_ops->isr(sess);
@@ -1185,6 +1194,9 @@ static irqreturn_t vdec_threaded_isr(int irq, void *data)
 	struct amvdec_core *core = data;
 	struct amvdec_session *sess = core->cur_sess;
 
+	if (!sess)
+		return IRQ_NONE;
+
 	return sess->fmt_out->codec_ops->threaded_isr(sess);
 }
 
